    <statement><p>Find the vector parameterization for the line which passes through <m>P = \left(6,1,10\right)</m> 
with direction vector <m>\mathbf{v} = \left\lt 3,-1,-1\right&gt;</m>.</p>
<p><var form="buttons">
<li>
<p><m>\left\lt 3t,-1t,-1t\right&gt;</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\left\lt 6+3t,1+\left(-1\right)t,10+\left(-1\right)t\right&gt;</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\left\lt 3+6t,-1+1t,-1+10t\right&gt;</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\left\lt 18,-1,-10\right&gt;</m></p>
</li>
</var></p>
</statement>
    <solution><m>f(t) = \overrightarrow{OP} + t * \mathbf{v} = \left\lt 6,1,10\right&gt; + \left\lt 3,-1,-1\right&gt; t = \left\lt 6+3t,1+\left(-1\right)t,10+\left(-1\right)t\right&gt;</m>


</solution>
